#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "c700cc22-203a-5ad3-913c-e5eb507e22e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13995" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}a+4b=1 \\\\ 2a+b=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $a$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$, \nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2},$ then the coefficient of $a$ will turn into $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n![](images/2b/2b0aa0d1dbfeb1e711bde6e7741fe5706aa126d71c44ae417d3c78d01b83547a.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2a}-8b & =-2 \\\\ \\cancel{2a}+b & =-5 \\\\ (-8b+b) & =(-2-5) \\\\ -7b & =-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2},$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "eb7f1f32-1a5c-526e-878b-8046c4feb8c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13997" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y=2 \\\\ x-2y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$, \nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $4,$ while in the second equation it is $-2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2},$ then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n![](images/0e/0e494f68d4859d46c3c369274e415f10a850c664343d41cce8dcfcfdd660e17c.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\cancel{4y} & =2 \\\\ 2x-\\cancel{4y} & =8 \\\\ (3x+2x) & =(2+8) \\\\ 5x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2},$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192587 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "f20f46d9-b799-57a2-90bc-12e6593e8655" :question/math-academy-id "e-13999" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=8 \\\\ x-2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n![](images/a7/a7e5f9f09d67dd14a4797e5675585973e3aafeb1ee96e9021d245f49ce9c1c7e.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2x}+3y & =8 \\\\ \\cancel{-2x}+4y & =6 \\\\ (3y+4y) & =(8+6) \\\\ 7y & =14 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 2.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y = 2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x-2y & =-3 \\\\ x-2(2) & =-3 \\\\ x-4 & =-3 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=1, \\,y=2,$ which can be expressed as $(1,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192588 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "238f847f-5009-5183-b9bd-b8e136f0ba4d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "990e3660-dfd7-50fa-b60b-0478ff02a073" :question/math-academy-id "e-14002" :question/problem "Find the solution $(u,v)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5u-6v=3 \\\\ -3u+2v=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $v$-coefficient in the first equation is $-6,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $3,$ then the $v$-coefficient will become $6,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the first equation.\n![](images/e7/e701d299976539abdbbe6e9c311c2db14c23cca6817c5a3de5b5c05a95760d99.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $v$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}5u-\\cancel{6v} & =3 \\\\ -9u+\\cancel{6v} & =-15 \\\\ (5u-9u) & =(3-15) \\\\ -4u & =-12 \\\\ u & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $u = 3.$ However, we still need to find $v.$ To do this, we substitute $u = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+2v & =-5 \\\\ -3(3)+2v & =-5 \\\\ -9+2v & =-5 \\\\ 2v & =4 \\\\ v & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u = 3, \\,v = 2,$ which can be expressed as $(3,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "238f847f-5009-5183-b9bd-b8e136f0ba4d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ff1fa4-ffc7-5336-b3af-c476f0ceefb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508536} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b6243-75d7-5af0-9491-17de5aeb8a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508553} {:answer/id #uuid "7e050490-5650-55a2-bbaf-c33b2adf2dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508573} {:answer/id #uuid "c386a187-6f74-5af7-a28a-842f181e5f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508690} {:answer/id #uuid "f8157de3-2831-5e1e-a4bb-0158173f239a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ff1fa4-ffc7-5336-b3af-c476f0ceefb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508536} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1429b72-180d-5d2a-ae39-57cc2cf7b25c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c472f9d-cfda-5414-a840-ee6d18544bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-170159" :question/problem "Find the solution $(p,q)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q=11 \\\\ 5p+4q=19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $q.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $q$-coefficient in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $4.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-2,$ then the $q$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,3p+2q=11\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 5p+4q=19\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-6p-4q=-22 \\\\ 5p+4q=19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $q$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-6p-\\cancel{4q} & =-22 \\\\ 5p+\\cancel{4q} & =19 \\\\ (-6p+5p) & =(-22+19) \\\\ -p & =-3 \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $p=3.$ However, we still need to find $q.$ To do this, we substitute $p=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p+2q & =11 \\\\ 3(3)+2q & =11 \\\\ 9+2q & =11 \\\\ 2q & =2 \\\\ q & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=3,\\,q=1,$ which can be expressed as $(3,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} {:answer/id #uuid "7891246f-146f-5da4-be15-343b7425f61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508564} {:answer/id #uuid "8468d23b-6f42-50bf-9e79-d910d35e0ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508587} {:answer/id #uuid "ac47150e-5e39-5c69-9314-ddb4609e8210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508651} {:answer/id #uuid "f55c1c33-5ff5-5f10-90f5-08f56a27906c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d02a81e-fa71-57d8-a298-b58e206ffcea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c0138a9-c275-57a0-80c9-430f32b2f421" :question/math-academy-id "q-18787" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ 2x-3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $x$-coefficient in the first equation is $4,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ (\\,2x-3y=2\\,)\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ -4x+6y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4x}-5y & =0 \\\\ -\\cancel{4x}+6y & =-4 \\\\ (-5y+6y) & =(0-4) \\\\ y & =-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=-4.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=-4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}4x-5y & =0 \\\\ 4x-5(-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x+20 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-20 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5,\\,y=-4,$ which can be expressed as $(-5,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a45b4e3-546f-58ce-bc86-f21f14be794d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191246} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce11990-8f77-5ca3-bb7c-924e6d9f7e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a45b4e3-546f-58ce-bc86-f21f14be794d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f741ca69-46ce-51d3-89ee-ebd3b9b5298e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2d6ae65-382f-5725-8d12-368b3161c220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191249} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dd37b2-c127-522c-8a0a-7efbd395282d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191250} {:answer/id #uuid "2d811e29-d735-5f20-b57d-488fa19f4d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191251} {:answer/id #uuid "43aa771d-f31e-507f-a36a-818c77be68a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5dd37b2-c127-522c-8a0a-7efbd395282d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191250} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2c168a-6d3a-5018-b549-be3fcba5455b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35ea5fbe-0a0e-53a6-8872-3cafe1bfb9c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-210859" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ s+5t=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $3,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $-3,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ (\\,s+5t=10\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ -3s-15t=-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3s}+4t & =8 \\\\ -\\cancel{3s}-15t & =-30 \\\\ (4t-15t) & =(8-30) \\\\ -11t & =-22 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-3,$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396c0c6a-1e03-5316-868c-3693041a6a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} {:answer/id #uuid "7405e912-7fbf-5e14-9ed1-9fa8aad46b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "396c0c6a-1e03-5316-868c-3693041a6a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d7b3eb-155c-54a4-84ac-4a02f7b9e7e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564482bf-2dea-55bc-82ec-61c16390e434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} {:answer/id #uuid "802cf47d-d04d-59cb-9afb-86ba6294bc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508578} {:answer/id #uuid "82dc65ea-5abd-5f0e-b1d6-8d53cd015c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508583} {:answer/id #uuid "ed089b80-c77d-5a59-8fbf-99ba45caaf88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "564482bf-2dea-55bc-82ec-61c16390e434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa84268-830c-548e-ba16-e867f14c3bf3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a68ca7c-dc16-5d70-b5c4-e7c98a96c8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-238035" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ 2x+5y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $10,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5,$ then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-10,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $10$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ (\\,2x+5y=-4\\,)\\,\\times (-5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ -10x-25y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{10x}-3y & =36 \\\\ -\\cancel{10x}-25y & =20 \\\\ (-3y-25y) & =(36+20) \\\\ -28y & =56 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-5,$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012d1788-aae6-5b3f-9a33-32cfe9441bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508392} {:answer/id #uuid "82649ab6-63e2-5e38-9a54-9307deefdeb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508581} {:answer/id #uuid "8b82b948-2752-5af9-8b4b-7dbe6940b437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508598} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e16c77-b35b-5b8b-82d8-51637fcbbe74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82649ab6-63e2-5e38-9a54-9307deefdeb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508581} :answer-field/id #uuid "4046a4d7-d1ee-512c-8f22-ac17abe07653" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58ca67c6-ef0f-5fd0-bbf0-abeced525206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508521} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9c819a-e67f-55f7-ae5e-0327e8b580c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58ca67c6-ef0f-5fd0-bbf0-abeced525206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508521} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e78a58b-7fed-5d4a-8336-150e88af3ff3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09338f11-6e50-5f7e-baa9-764c66288045" :question/math-academy-id "q-238044" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+y=8 \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $y,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $-7.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $7,$ then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $7,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $-7$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-5x+y=8\\,)\\,\\times (7) \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-35x+7y=56 \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-35x+\\cancel{7y} & =56 \\\\ 8x-\\cancel{7y} & =25 \\\\ (-35x+8x) & =(56+25) \\\\ -27x & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\text{first}$ equation by $7,$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184b7ab4-4868-5106-9bdf-4e1438c33364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508425} {:answer/id #uuid "4662f5b1-a02f-591b-952a-acc6e7eaed94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508495} {:answer/id #uuid "62b5b5df-e1f1-5779-aade-7a55fb1642e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508539} {:answer/id #uuid "bffa8226-fe91-5e80-8884-d0fbe91ee966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b5b5df-e1f1-5779-aade-7a55fb1642e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508539} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d35b8c-5919-5861-973d-60696f665ffd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a15f6018-6390-5ae8-8699-d85026a934d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508631} {:answer/id #uuid "aea80158-002e-503d-aa81-d682984720c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a15f6018-6390-5ae8-8699-d85026a934d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508631} :answer-field/id #uuid "6752cba9-1654-5c73-9d09-080f3eb8532e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ba7c176-1d51-52ad-ad1b-a588df23024a" :question/math-academy-id "q-238051" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q=11 \\\\ p+q=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $q$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $q,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $q$ in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the coefficient of $q$ will turn into $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q=11 \\\\ (\\,p+q=4\\,)\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q=11 \\\\ -2p-2q=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $q$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3p+\\cancel{2q} & =11 \\\\ -2p-\\cancel{2q} & =-8 \\\\ (3p-2p) & =(11-8) \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $q,$ multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-2,$ and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dddb3dd-6633-5329-a169-4b39e35735ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dddb3dd-6633-5329-a169-4b39e35735ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628} :answer-field/id #uuid "2696769d-e344-58f2-b122-e8524fb62262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5032cf38-f7e1-5f19-b56e-8d84bbbcec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5032cf38-f7e1-5f19-b56e-8d84bbbcec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509} :answer-field/id #uuid "2adc4195-f1d2-500e-8a09-82e4a8b25e53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4775db8b-54b5-507a-83b4-6fee15253323" :question/math-academy-id "q-238082" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ 2x+6y=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y)$ to this system is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the  first  equation is $6,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-6,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ (\\,2x+6y=12\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ -6x-18y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{6x}+13y & =21 \\\\ -\\cancel{6x}-18y & =-36 \\\\ (13y-18y) & =(21-36) \\\\ -5y & =-15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=3.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+13y & =21 \\\\ 6x+13(3) & =21 \\\\ 6x+39 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =-18 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=3,$ which can be expressed as $(-3,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "238f847f-5009-5183-b9bd-b8e136f0ba4d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5deaa590-2cc0-5e91-b357-5a9ea981fe20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5deaa590-2cc0-5e91-b357-5a9ea981fe20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508529} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fdb15c-a8b3-5277-abc3-5f3c2cfa726d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e8f613-08b6-5743-b480-77cc2a7e2ff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6e8f613-08b6-5743-b480-77cc2a7e2ff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508699} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2a4186-c9b8-58ca-9163-304a07832933" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "659bfd82-a0b2-5112-81eb-2185b857af31" :question/math-academy-id "q-238087" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y=11 \\\\ 7x+4y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y.$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $4.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-2,$ then the $y$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-5x+2y=11\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 7x+4y=5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-4y=-22 \\\\ 7x+4y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-\\cancel{4y} & =-22 \\\\ 7x+\\cancel{4y} & =5 \\\\ (10x+7x) & =(-22+5) \\\\ 17x & =-17 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=-1.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=-1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+4y & =5 \\\\ 7(-1)+4y & =5 \\\\ -7+4y & =5 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1,\\,y=3,$ which can be expressed as $(-1,3).$"}]}
